  m_Name: SnowDoor
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: SafeHaven::RaidEventDefinition
  id: rumour.snowdoor
  displayName: The Door in the Snow
  weight: 1
  earliestSeconds: 90
  latestSecondsLeft: 90
  minimumStage: 0
  warning: 
  warningSound: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ad5c451edd0edde49967af502c90ec94, type: 2}
  sitePrefab: {fileID: 6647756069553415008, guid: b5ee6030ac379034ab24d00d35614ff8, type: 3}
  siteDistance: {x: 35, y: 70}
  siteText: A stone door stands on its own in a snow hollow, framed in rock as dark as the portal's, a seam of silver light down its face. The snow round it falls upward. A man in a grey cloak kneels with his palm to the stone. "It has her voice," he says, without looking round.
  artwork: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 390f841f37daf3f4c96afdc728c3344d, type: 3}
  onStart: []
  choices:
  - label: Let him try the door
    detail: He wants it so badly. Something may come through with the voice.
    cost: []
    result: The seam widens. A voice says his name, and he flinches, because the one he is looking for never used it. Things come out behind the voice.
    outcomes:
    - rid: 2623126268168110227
    - rid: 2623126268168110228
  - label: Hold the lantern to it
    detail: It ends here. He won't thank you, not yet.
    cost: []
    result: Green-gold light runs along the frame, and whatever was pressing at the seam draws back. "I could have watched you feed it another name," he says.
    outcomes: []
  raisesWhenChosen: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8251127e62e64b542b5653a1d2c0962d, type: 2}
